{% set local_problem %}
<p>Alabama's humidity takes a toll on fascia boards, and Priceville homes are no exception. When gutters clog or leak, water runs behind them and soaks into the fascia. In our humid climate, that moisture creates perfect conditions for rot, mold, and wood-destroying insects.</p>

<p>Newer Priceville construction isn't immune — builder-grade materials and rushed installation can leave fascia vulnerable from day one. And established homes throughout the area have weathered decades of exposure, with many showing signs of water damage along the roofline.</p>

<p>We've worked on homes throughout Morgan County long enough to know that fascia problems are common — and commonly missed. Homeowners call about gutter issues, and we find that the real problem is the rotted wood behind the gutters. You can't fix the gutter problem without fixing the fascia first.</p>

<p>The good news: caught early, fascia repair is straightforward and affordable. Left alone, rot spreads to rafters and roof structure — turning a manageable repair into a major project.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>We start with a thorough inspection, checking fascia and soffit for water damage, soft spots, and rot. We'll show you exactly what we find and explain what needs repair — no exaggeration, no unnecessary work.</p>

<p>For damaged sections, we carefully remove existing gutters, cut out the rotted wood back to solid material, and install new fascia boards. We use quality primed lumber or composite materials designed for our humid climate.</p>

<p>Everything is properly sealed and prepared for gutter installation. Then we install your new seamless gutters on the fresh fascia — properly attached, properly sloped, and designed to prevent the overflow that caused the rot in the first place.</p>
{% endset %}

